  "english": "Prophet Isaiah 10:12 \"And it shall come to pass...\" to verse 19 \"...shall write them down.\"\nThe Apostle, 2 Corinthians 2:12 \"Furthermore, when I came...\" to 3:3 \"...[but on] tablets of flesh.\"\nAlleluia of the Resurrection, according to the tone.\nGospel Mark 6:30 \"Then the apostles gathered...\" to verse 44 \"...five thousand [men].\"\n\nMonday. Of the Saints: Andrew the General and his army, and the Witnesses [Martyrs] Callinicus and Diomedes.\nPatristic Hymn [Harts], Tone 6 [gki]: \"The heavenly hosts...\" (Zinvorutyunk).\nMidday Psalm 5 [6]: \"Lord, as with a shield...\"\nProverbs 4:10 \"Hear, my son...\" to verse 27 \"...shall make your ways straight.\"\nProphet Isaiah 48:17 \"Thus says the Lord...\" to verse 21 \"...for the wicked, says the Lord.\"\nThe Apostle, 2 Corinthians 10:3 \"For though we walk...\" to verse 6 \"...is fulfilled.\"\nAlleluia of the Martyrs, according to the tone.\nGospel Matthew 10:37 \"He who loves father...\" to verse 42 \"...his reward.\"\n\nTuesday. Of the Saints: Adrian and his wife Anatolia, and the Martyrs Theodore and Eleutherius.\nPatristic Hymn [Harts] of the Martyrs.\nMidday Psalm 115 [116]: \"Precious in the sight of the Lord...\"\nProphet Jeremiah, Lamentations 3:22 \"Through the Lord's mercies...\" to verse 56 \"...my voice\" (it is an excerpt).\nThe Apostle, Romans 8:18 \"For I consider...\" to verse 27 \"...for the saints.\"\nAlleluia of the Martyrs, according to the tone.\nGospel John 16:1 \"These things I have spoken...\" to verse 5 \"...I was with you.\"\n\nWednesday. Patristic Hymn [Harts] of Repentance.\nMidday Psalm 85 [86]: \"Save Your servant...\"\nThe Apostle, 2 Corinthians 1:12 \"For our boasting...\" to verse 22 \"...in our hearts.\"\nAlleluia of the Fast, according to the tone.\nGospel Mark 5:35 \"While He was still speaking...\" to verse 43 \"...[something] should be given her to eat.\"\n\n[Unreadable text/scribble line]\n\nThursday. Of the Saints: Abraham and Khoren, and the unmercenary physicians Cosmas and Damian, and the martyr Adeodatus [Astvatsatur].\n(Their commemoration index is at the end; first look at the main feasts above.)\n\nFriday. Patristic Hymn [Harts] of Rest.\nMidday Psalm 97 [98]: \"All [the ends of the earth] have seen...\"\nThe Apostle, 2 Corinthians 1:23 \"Moreover I call God as witness...\" to 2:11 \"...of his devices.\"\nAlleluia of the Fast, according to the tone.\nGospel Mark 6:1 \"Then He went out from there...\" to verse 6 \"...because of their unbelief.\"\n\nSaturday. Feast of the Birth of the Holy Mother of God from Anna, or of the Holy Council of Nicaea.\n(For on this Saturday, one of these two feasts is necessarily celebrated according to the directory of the calendar year.)\n\nBut on the Sunday of the Eve [Barekendan], Patristic Hymn [Harts], Tone 6 [gki]: \"Ineffable...\" (Anchareli).\nMidday Psalm 64 [65]: \"Praise awaits You...\"\nProphet Isaiah 14:1 \"Thus says the Lord...\" to verse 11 \"...I will bring low.\"\nThe Apostle, 2 Corinthians 7:4 \"Great is my boldness...\" to verse 16 \"...I have confidence in you.\"\nAlleluia of the Resurrection, according to the tone.\nGospel Mark 7:31 \"And again, departing...\" to verse 37 \"...and the mute to speak.\"\n\nCanon of the Birth of the Holy Virgin.\nNow, the Feast of the Birth of the Holy Virgin Mary, Mother of God, from Anna is placed here, which is always celebrated on September 8.\nIn the evening, perform a pre-festal service [Nakhatonak], Tone 1 [aki]: \"Who foreknew...\" (Nor nakhimats), with its proper variables.\nAnd during the night office, Canticle [Hambartsi], Tone 6 [gki]: \"Sing, sons of Zion...\" (Yerketsek vordik sioni), with its proper variables.\nSong: \"He shall come down like rain.\"\nLitany: \"Holy Mother.\"\n\"Holy God,\" who wast crucified.\nAfter that, Psalm 67 [68]: \"The Lord gave the word...\" Response [Pokh]: \"Let God arise.\"\nProverbs 31:29 \"Many daughters...\" to verse 31 \"...forever.\"\nProphet Isaiah 61:9 \"Thus says the Lord...\" to verse 9 \"...shall be in the Lord.\"\nThe Apostle, Galatians 3:24 \"Therefore the law...\" to verse 29 \"...heirs.\"\nAlleluia: \"Rejoice, O favored one.\"\nGospel Matthew 1:1 \"The book of the genealogy of Jesus Christ...\" to verse 17 \"...fourteen generations.\"\nSong, as appropriate: \"Creator of All\" (Ararchakan); and if it be Sunday: \"Newly Created\" (Norasteghtsyal).\nLitany: \"Let us ask...\" \"Save [us].\"\nPrayer: \"To Your all-powerful...\" (Koum amenazor).\n\nAt Midday, Introit [Zhamamut]: \"We beseech you...\" Response [Pokh]: \"My soul magnifies...\"\nHymn [Sharakan], Tone 6 [gki]: \"Tree of Life.\"\nAnd then read the scriptures of the day. Holy [Sacrifice]—",
